From: Bonesaw personal loot (#114) <core-patch 0029>
Subject: [PATCH 0029] personal loot: bypass shared/group loot rules

NOTE: 0029 may collide with a parallel agent landing 0029; parent renumbers
at commit time.

WHAT
----
Issue #114: players must never roll or fight over drops. All loot becomes
personal: every eligible group member can loot every item of a kill/chest
independently, first come first served. No Need/Greed rolls, no Master
Looter distribution, no Round Robin ownership.

CHOSEN SEMANTICS (precise)
--------------------------
Not per-member duplicate world drops. Each item still drops ONCE from the
single shared Loot object; the change only changes WHO MAY LOOT:

- A new Group::GetEffectiveLootMethod() returns FREE_FOR_ALL instead of
  ROUND_ROBIN / MASTER_LOOT / GROUP_LOOT / NEED_BEFORE_GREED whenever the
  worldserver config option "Loot.PersonalLootAll" is true (default ON,
  registered as CONFIG_PERSONAL_LOOT_ALL). FREE_FOR_ALL and PERSONAL_LOOT
  pass through unchanged.
- All loot-decision call sites now consult GetEffectiveLootMethod() instead
  of GetLootMethod():
  * Player.cpp creature + gameobject chest loot-open switches -> the
    Group::GroupLoot / NeedBeforeGreed / MasterLoot roll machinery is never
    entered, so no rolls ever start.
  * Player.cpp loot permission switch -> every group member gets
    ALL_PERMISSION (sees and may take everything), instead of
    MASTER/RESTRICTED/GROUP/ROUND_ROBIN permissions.
  * Player::isAllowedToLoot (PlayerStorage.cpp) -> any group member may open
    the corpse like FFA.
  * Player::StoreLootItem exploit-protection (Player.cpp ~13874) -> the
    master-looter-only guard never applies.
  * WorldSession::HandleLootMasterGive (LootHandler.cpp) -> master-give
    packets are rejected even if the group's stored method is Master Loot.
- The group's stored m_lootMethod (persisted in characters DB, shown in the
  client group UI) is untouched; only loot behaviour is overridden.
- Money is unaffected: HandleLootMoneyOpcode already splits gold equally to
  all members within loot-reward distance for any group method.
- Quest items / conditional items are untouched: they already flow through
  per-player views (PlayerQuestItems / PlayerNonQuestNonFFAConditionalItems
  filled by Loot::FillNotNormalLootFor for every member at FillLoot time),
  which is exactly the existing per-player duplication AzerothCore uses for
  FFA.
- Playerbots loot through the same player loot paths and are unaffected
  beyond no longer needing to answer rolls.

WHY THIS MECHANISM
------------------
AzerothCore's FREE_FOR_ALL path IS the per-player loot view (ALL_PERMISSION
+ per-player FFA/quest/conditional lists); routing every shared method into
it reuses proven code instead of duplicating LootItems per member.

FILES
-----
 src/server/game/World/WorldConfig.h          | add CONFIG_PERSONAL_LOOT_ALL
 src/server/game/World/WorldConfig.cpp        | register Loot.PersonalLootAll (true)
 src/server/game/Groups/Group.h               | declare GetEffectiveLootMethod()
 src/server/game/Groups/Group.cpp             | implement GetEffectiveLootMethod()
 src/server/game/Entities/Player/Player.cpp   | 4 call sites -> effective method
 src/server/game/Entities/Player/PlayerStorage.cpp | isAllowedToLoot
 src/server/game/Handlers/LootHandler.cpp     | HandleLootMasterGive guard
---
--- a/src/server/game/Groups/Group.h
+++ b/src/server/game/Groups/Group.h
@@ -230,6 +230,12 @@
     ObjectGuid GetGUID() const;
     char const* GetLeaderName() const;
     LootMethod GetLootMethod() const;
+    // Loot method with the personal-loot override applied: when
+    // CONFIG_PERSONAL_LOOT_ALL ("Loot.PersonalLootAll", default true) is on,
+    // every shared/group method (Round Robin, Master Loot, Group Loot,
+    // Need Before Greed) reads as FREE_FOR_ALL so all loot is lootable
+    // personally by every eligible member - no rolls, no master looter.
+    LootMethod GetEffectiveLootMethod() const;
     ObjectGuid GetLooterGuid() const;
     ObjectGuid GetMasterLooterGuid() const;
     ItemQualities GetLootThreshold() const;
--- a/src/server/game/Groups/Group.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Groups/Group.cpp
@@ -2628,6 +2628,29 @@
     return m_lootMethod;
 }
 
+LootMethod Group::GetEffectiveLootMethod() const
+{
+    // Personal loot (#114): when enabled, bypass all shared/group loot rules -
+    // every method behaves as FREE_FOR_ALL (each member may loot everything
+    // personally, first come first served; no rolls, no master looter).
+    // FREE_FOR_ALL and PERSONAL_LOOT are already personal and pass through.
+    if (sWorld->getBoolConfig(CONFIG_PERSONAL_LOOT_ALL))
+    {
+        switch (m_lootMethod)
+        {
+            case ROUND_ROBIN:
+            case MASTER_LOOT:
+            case GROUP_LOOT:
+            case NEED_BEFORE_GREED:
+                return FREE_FOR_ALL;
+            default:
+                break;
+        }
+    }
+
+    return m_lootMethod;
+}
+
 ObjectGuid Group::GetLooterGuid() const
 {
     return m_looterGuid;
